WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:00.867
So is it going?

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.969
Hundreds of additional forces to Kosovo

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.371
following Monday's clashes

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.939
with Serbian protesters

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:08.108
in the northern part of the country.

00:00:08.108 --> 00:00:09.175
NATO commander

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.211
called the deployment of forces to Kosovo

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:13.179
a prudent measure

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.848
would ensure NATO's Kosovo

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:15.482
force, known

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.783
as KFOR,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.018
would have the capabilities

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.120
to maintain security.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.555
30 NATO peacekeepers in the Kosovo Air

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.523
Force were injured

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.125
during Monday's clashes.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.092
Kosovo's prime minister

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.694
condemned the protesters,

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.595
telling CNN

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.630
he would not surrender his country

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:33.233
to what he called a fascist militia.

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.771
We are facing not peaceful protesters

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.540
who are facing a mob of extremists,

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.143
who are facing ultranationalist

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.544
right wingers

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.112
who are being paid

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:49.682
and ordered from Belgrade and who admire

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.819
despotic President Putin.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:53.820
Meantime, Serbia's

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.821
president is expressing

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.589
concern for the survival

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.658
and security of Serbs in Kosovo.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.926
Monday's clashes

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:00.460
took place

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.395
in the northern part of Kosovo,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.131
which is a majority Kosovo Serb area.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.367
Officials from the U.S., NATO

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.135
and the European Union

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.437
condemned the violence

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:12.038
against NATO's peacekeepers

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:13.339
and called on both sides to

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.941
de-escalate tensions.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.812
It has been too much violence.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.015
We have too much violence in Europe

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.683
already today.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.219
We cannot afford another conflict

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:28.988
For more on this story, Hughes

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.458
Barbie Nadeau, who grew

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.363
a flare up in a tinderbox

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.532
More than 30 NATO's peacekeepers

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.700
injured in clashes

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.935
with Serb protesters

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.170
in northern Kosovo Monday.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:44.904
Among them,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.040
several Italians and Hungarians

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.777
Naito has condemned the attacks,

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.045
saying they were, quote,

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:55.281
totally unacceptable.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.517
The peacekeepers known as KFOR

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.551
have been present

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.521
in this volatile region since 1999

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.422
in response

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.824
to brutal ethnic cleansing of Albanians

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.059
The U.N.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:07.894
Security Council passed a resolution

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.062
after a United Nations

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:09.963
Security Council

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.030
resolution pave

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.765
the way for Kosovo's independence

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:13.766
from Serbia.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:14.434
With NATO's

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.469
protecting the uneasy transition.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:21.007
Former test for Kosovo

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.275
declared its independence

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.444
from Serbia in 2008,

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:25.712
with the ethnic Albanian

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.614
majority took over the country.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:29.949
But Serbia did

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:30.850
not recognize

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.052
Kosovo as a sovereign nation,

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.420
nor do ethnic Serbs

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.955
who live in the north of the country

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:39.325
where Monday's violence sparked.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.493
Nor does Russia,

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.628
which has strongly backed

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.963
Serbia over Kosovo.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:44.731
Consider

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.168
the latest tension comes after ethnic

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.869
Serbs boycotted an election

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.971
in the northern part of Kosovo in April,

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:52.839
leading to

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.275
ethnic Albanians governing the region.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:57.677
Serbia claims

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.845
the Kosovo government

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:01.247
is goading Serbs to clash with NATO's

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.150
Serbian across the remit of Islam.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.985
I am urging the Serbs in Kosovo

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.021
not to get into a conflict with Netto,

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.223
not because I'm afraid

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.192
or because any of us are afraid.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.193
None of us personally

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:14.761
have anything to lose.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.562
But because that's

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.031
what Kosovo's prime minister wants most.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.233
Nicholas needs to,

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.201
as peacekeepers,

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.102
stand guard inspection today,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.571
whether the protesters here,

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.139
listen, could determine

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.307
whether relative peace

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.008
returns to the region

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.010
or if Europe has another conflict

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.878
on the horizon.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:33.880
Barbie

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.350
Nadeau, CNN, Rome.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.551
To do more into this story,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:41.120
I'm joined by Matthew kind of via

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.456
Skype from Bratislava, Slovakia.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.991
He's the chief Europe

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.559
correspondent for Politico.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.695
Matthew, great to have you with us.

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.331
Tell us, have these the these tensions

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.733
been brewing for a while

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.704
Well, thanks for having me.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:58.871
And you're absolutely right.

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.173
These tensions

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:02.575
